19164      title 'Comparing PROC GAM with PROC GENMOD';
19165      data kyphosis;
19166      input Age StartVert NumVert Kyphosis @@;
19167      datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.KYPHOSIS has 83 observations and 4 variables.

19196      ;
19197      proc genmod data=kyphosis descending;
19198      model Kyphosis = Age StartVert NumVert/link=logit dist=binomial;
19199      run;

NOTE: PROC GENMOD is modeling the probability that Kyphosis='1'.
NOTE: The Pearson chi-square and deviance are not computed since the AGGREGATE option is not specified.
NOTE: Algorithm converged.
NOTE: The scale parameter was held fixed.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE GENMOD printed page 2316.

19200      title 'Comparing PROC GAM with PROC GENMOD';
19201      proc gam data=kyphosis;
19202      model Kyphosis (event='1') = spline(Age ,df=3)
19203      spline(StartVert,df=3)
19204      spline(NumVert ,df=3) / dist=binomial;
19205      run;

NOTE: PROC GAM is modeling the probability that Kyphosis=1. One way to change this to model the probability that Kyphosis=0 is to specify the response variable 
      option EVENT='0'.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE GAM printed page 2317.

19206      title 'PROC GAM with Approximate Analysis of Deviance';
19207      proc gam data=kyphosis;
19208      model Kyphosis (event='1') = spline(Age ,df=3)
19209      spline(StartVert,df=3)
19210      spline(NumVert ,df=3) /
19211      dist=binomial anodev=norefit;
19212      run;

NOTE: PROC GAM is modeling the probability that Kyphosis=1. One way to change this to model the probability that Kyphosis=0 is to specify the response variable 
